\pard\qc\b\fs34 Ubitron Mobility Axiom\par
\pard\qc\b\fs28 User Manual\par
\pard\qc\fs20 Audience: Operators, dispatchers, supervisors, evidence staff\par
\pard\qc\fs20 Language: English\par
\pard\qc\fs20 Version 1.1\par
\pard\qc\fs20 Revision date: July 2026\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 1. About this manual\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard This manual explains daily use of Mobility Axiom: sign-in, \b Operations\b0 , live video, \b PTT\b0 , SOS, messages, evidence, and the other main tabs.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard It does not cover server install, firewall, or license files. Ask your administrator for those topics.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard Related: Quick Start Guide (first day) · ask IT for Installation / Technical manuals.\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 2. Before you start\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard 1. Dashboard address from your administrator\par
\pard 2. Your username and password\par
\pard 3. Chrome or Edge\par
\pard 4. At least one online body-worn camera when you test live features\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Login page]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 3. Sign in\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Enter the dashboard with your operator account.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b IMPORTANT \emdash First sign-in (new install only)\par
\pard 1. On a brand-new server, IT may give you \b global\b0  / \b global123\b0  once.\par
\pard 2. After \b Sign in\b0 , the screen \b Change your password\b0  appears. You cannot keep the factory password.\par
\pard 3. Rules: at least 12 characters, with upper case, lower case, a number, and a symbol. Type the new password; do not paste.\par
\pard 4. Click \b Save and continue\b0 , then sign in again with \b global\b0  and your new password.\par
\pard 5. \b global123\b0  stops working. Store the new password safely or ask IT if your site uses named operator accounts instead.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps (all users)\par
\pard 1. Open Chrome or Edge.\par
\pard 2. Enter the dashboard address from your administrator.\par
\pard 3. Enter \b Username\b0 .\par
\pard 4. Enter \b Password\b0 .\par
\pard 5. Choose \b Language\b0  if needed.\par
\pard 6. Click \b Sign in\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps \emdash Change your password (new install)\par
\pard 1. Confirm you are on \b Change your password\b0 .\par
\pard 2. In \b Current password\b0 , type the install password (\b global123\b0  on a new server).\par
\pard 3. In \b New password\b0 , type a password that meets every rule on screen.\par
\pard 4. In \b Confirm new password\b0 , type it again.\par
\pard 5. Click \b Save and continue\b0 .\par
\pard 6. Sign in again with \b global\b0  and the new password.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard Returning site: dashboard opens.\par
\pard New install: \b Change your password\b0  first, then dashboard after the second sign-in.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Common problems\par
\pard 1. Stuck on \b Change your password\b0  \emdash meet all rules; you cannot keep \b global123\b0 .\par
\pard 2. \b global123\b0  rejected \emdash normal after first change; use your new password.\par
\pard 3. No factory hint on the login page \emdash normal on sites that already changed the install password.\par
\pard 4. Login rejected \emdash check spelling, Caps Lock, and saved browser passwords.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Sign in form]\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Change your password]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 4. Change language\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Open the \b Language\b0  selector.\par
\pard 2. Choose the language you need.\par
\pard 3. Confirm labels update.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Language selector]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 5. Main tabs\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard Your role may hide some tabs. Exact names:\par
\pard 1. \b Operations\b0  \emdash map, devices, live wall, SOS, \b PTT\b0 , messages\par
\pard 2. \b Evidence & Docking\b0  \emdash library, docks, exports, storage (IT)\par
\pard 3. \b Command Wall\b0  \emdash large multi-panel live wall\par
\pard 4. \b Centre Summary\b0  \emdash site summary views\par
\pard 5. \b Video Conference\b0  \emdash conference rooms (if licensed)\par
\pard 6. \b Settings\b0  \emdash options your role allows\par
\pard 7. \b Analytics\b0  \emdash analytics modules (if licensed)\par
\pard 8. \b CAD / RMS\b0  (Computer-Aided Dispatch / Records Management) \emdash optional integration for incident dispatch and records when licensed\par
\pard 9. \b Tactical\b0  \emdash tactical workspace (if licensed)\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Top navigation]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 6. Operations overview\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard \b Operations\b0  is the main control-room screen for live work.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard Typical layout:\par
\pard 1. Left: \b Devices\b0  list, SOS, PTT groups, \b Messages\b0\par
\pard 2. Centre: live map\par
\pard 3. Right: live video wall panels\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Operations with Devices, map, and wall labeled]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 7. Devices list\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Find units and start Pin, PTT, or Call.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Open \b Operations\b0 .\par
\pard 2. Use the \b Devices\b0  list.\par
\pard 3. Filter with \b Online only\b0  or search by name or ID if needed.\par
\pard 4. Confirm \b Status\b0  shows \b Online\b0  before live actions.\par
\pard 5. Use row actions: \b Pin\b0 , \b PTT\b0 , \b Call\b0  (and GPS tools when shown).\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Notes\par
\pard 1. \b Open All (Up to 8)\b0  opens several online units when your role allows it.\par
\pard 2. If the list is empty, ask your administrator \emdash devices are registered by IT.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Devices row with Pin, PTT, Call]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 8. Open live video (Pin)\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Watch a body-worn camera live on the map.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Open \b Operations\b0 .\par
\pard 2. Find an \b Online\b0  device in \b Devices\b0 .\par
\pard 3. Click \b Pin\b0 .\par
\pard 4. Wait for the live panel on the map.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard Live video appears for that unit.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Common problems\par
\pard 1. Device Offline \emdash wait or ask IT.\par
\pard 2. Panel opens but picture is slow \emdash wait a few seconds, then retry \b Pin\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Live pin panel]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 9. Use PTT\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Speak to a unit while you hold the button.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Find the unit in \b Devices\b0  or on the map panel.\par
\pard 2. Press and hold \b PTT\b0 .\par
\pard 3. Speak clearly.\par
\pard 4. Release \b PTT\b0  to stop.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard Audio goes out only while you hold \b PTT\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Important\par
\pard Do not tap \b PTT\b0 . Hold it.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: PTT control]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 10. Use Call\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Start a voice call session (no video) with a unit.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Find the unit.\par
\pard 2. Click \b Call\b0 .\par
\pard 3. Wait for answer per your SOP.\par
\pard 4. End the call when finished.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Call on Devices row]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 11. Respond to SOS\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard See an SOS alert and complete acknowledgement per site policy.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Read the red SOS banner (for example officer distress or fall alert text shown on screen).\par
\pard 2. Open live video with \b Pin\b0  if needed.\par
\pard 3. Check map position.\par
\pard 4. Adjust response radius only if your SOP uses that control.\par
\pard 5. Click \b Acknowledge\b0  when ready to record the response.\par
\pard 6. On \b SOS Acknowledgement\b0 , complete the on-screen fields (what happened, units involved, picture options as shown).\par
\pard 7. Click \b Submit & close\b0  when your policy says the incident can close.\par
\pard 8. Use \b PTT\b0  or \b Call\b0  for field direction as required.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard The SOS is acknowledged and logged according to the form you submitted.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: SOS banner]\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: SOS Acknowledgement]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 12. Send messages\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. On \b Operations\b0 , open \b Messages\b0 .\par
\pard 2. Select an online unit.\par
\pard 3. Type the message.\par
\pard 4. Click \b Send\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Messages panel]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 13. Use the map\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. On \b Operations\b0 , review live pins.\par
\pard 2. Click a pin for detail or live panel.\par
\pard 3. Use map tools (for example \b Fit pins\b0 ) only when needed.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Map with pins]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 14. Operations live wall\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Watch several live panels on the right side of \b Operations\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Open \b Operations\b0 .\par
\pard 2. Review the live wall panels.\par
\pard 3. Use \b Auto-rotate\b0 , \b Popout Matrix\b0 , or \b Config\b0  when your role allows it.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Notes\par
\pard \b Config\b0  assigns cameras to panels. It does not replace \b Pin\b0  for a single map live view.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Operations live wall]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 15. Evidence & Docking\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Find and review recorded evidence. Some storage tools are IT-only.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps \emdash open the hub\par
\pard 1. Open the \b Evidence & Docking\b0  tab.\par
\pard 2. Use the left navigation when shown:\par
\pard    a. \b Overview\b0\par
\pard    b. \b Evidence Library\b0\par
\pard    c. \b Case Files\b0\par
\pard    d. \b Docking Stations\b0\par
\pard    e. \b Export Approvals\b0  (often super admin)\par
\pard    f. \b Redacted exports\b0  / \b Investigation holds\b0  when licensed and shown\par
\pard    g. \b Storage\b0  (paths \emdash usually IT / super admin)\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps \emdash find a file\par
\pard 1. Open \b Evidence Library\b0 .\par
\pard 2. Search or filter for the file.\par
\pard 3. Open the file to review.\par
\pard 4. If the recording is missing, ask a super administrator (index or dock upload may need IT).\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Notes\par
\pard 1. Priority for operators: search \b Evidence Library\b0  first.\par
\pard 2. Do not change \b Storage\b0  paths unless you are authorised IT.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Evidence Library]\par
\pard\sa360\par

